        which writes the AI side as <strong>A</strong>, and the <strong>AI form</strong>, which
        writes it as <strong>AI</strong>: AI · AI–Hᵉ · AI&gt;H · AI=H / H=AI · H&gt;AI · H–AIᵉ ·
        H. They are identical in colour, geometry and meaning, differing in that one token; the
        human side is untouched at every tier, as are the split-ring order rule and the two
        co-authorship orderings. Both styles are part of the standard and its CC BY 4.0
        licence, and an adopter may display either, or both.
        <em>
